  "injuries": "Injury report from the league's official practice reports via nflverse: shown, not applied. The model reads only who starts at quarterback.",
  "lines": "Model line and model total are the model's own numbers beside the market's. Taking the model's side against the closing spread won 49.8% of 2016-2025 games and against the total 50.1%; -110 needs 52.4% to break even.",
  "model": "The pick is the model blended with the betting market. The market is hard to beat in the NFL: across 2016-2025 the blend picked 66.4% of winners against the closing favourite's 66.6%, and betting the model where it disagreed with the price lost money. Treat a pick as an opinion with a measured hit rate, not an edge.",
  "news": "Headlines from public NFL news feeds that name one of the two teams or their players, published before kickoff. Shown, not applied.",
  "players": "Most valuable on offence is ranked by expected points added (EPA) this season - the points a player's plays added above an average play in the same situation; defenders by sacks, takeaways, passes defended and tackles for loss. A listed player who is out or doubtful - or the most valuable player questionable - is flagged at the top of the game, from the official injury report and the weekly roster. Shown, not applied: only the starting quarterback moves the pick.",
  "props": "Projected yards are the middle of what the player's recent usage and his team's expected points point to, if he plays. In 2020-2025: passing 56 yards off on average (his own average: 67); rushing 18 yards off on average (his own average: 18); receiving 18 yards off on average (his own average: 20). Players went over about half the time, as a middle number should. Shown, not applied.",
  "qb": "The quarterback the model assumes is the one the schedule projects to start. If the injury report says he is out, the number above does not know yet.",
  "td": "Chance of a rushing or receiving touchdown, if he plays - from his recent carries, targets and snaps and his team's expected points from the betting line. In 2020-2025 each team's most likely scorer scored 43.5% of the time (the model said 41.1%). Measured, and shown, not applied.",
  "tiers": "STRONG, SOLID, LEAN and TOSS-UP are bands of the pick's probability. The percentage beside each is how often picks in that band won in 2016-2025 - measured, not promised.",
  "value_off": "No game is labelled a bet: backing the model where it disagreed with the closing moneyline did not make money in 2016-2025 at any edge tested."
